emucap: keep a yielded RSP running and deliver its SET_INTR interrupts.

When the RSP plugin returns without halting (cxd4 yields after the microcode writes SET_INTR,
or after polling SP_STATUS while it waits for the CPU), 2.6.0 marks the task locked, drops the
interrupt unless INTR_BREAK is set, and resumes the RSP only on the next CPU write to SP_STATUS.
libdragon's rspq signals syncpoints with SET_INTR (INTR_BREAK off) and expects the RSP to keep
running, so rspq_syncpoint_wait timed out. Signal the RSP-raised interrupt immediately, resume
the yielded task from an SP event, and leave a task that broke without a completion event halted.

